{"baseRefOid":"3a0251874d6ab38008173a22ef09d651a0f20d9e","body":"K6b's W1 memory estimate missed live allocations in retained-precision phases, and the numerical-robustness harness carried a stale copy. This shares one checked kernel envelope and composes each harness's caller allocations from the actual model and launch context. Admission holds now precede model-specific count prepasses. Solver semantics and protected numerical criteria are unchanged.\n\nThe evidence includes phase derivations, mutation controls, ordinary-artifact qualification, historical admission replay, and the completed post-KF3 W1-T4 schedule. The owner-approved comparison preserves available historical facts and the unchanged exact analytic checks; complete historical published-value equality remains unclaimed. The complete new published outputs are preserved.\n\nLimits remain explicit: the heap claim applies to the qualified profiles and matched measurement windows; eight RSS forecast misses inform the later W1 limits decision. TREE reached 512/1024-bit attempts without publication; precision-isolated heap peaks are unavailable. Historical VR launch qualifications, the T1 monitoring deviation and T2 outcome correction remain attached to their evidence.\n\nValidation: fresh independent source/records and final-head gate confirmation report no actionable finding. GEN-8, all five hosted runs and full-SHA dispatch37034799536 pass. Corrected Mac DEC-025 covers all40 manifests with only the same three baseline platform failures; Python, wasm, desktop tests and production build pass. The initial shared-target invocation error, failed attempt and corrected full rerun are preserved. T9/both-entry are inapplicable to this harness/validation-only slice. ROOT W1 limits and F2a remain subsequent work.\n\n[Independent final gate confirmation](https://github.com/sgttomas/chirality/blob/c0a86dc0f4b4e3787c48dbaa6b9c6852cb06acad/projects/chirality-piping/execution/_Coordination/AgentRuns/HELP-HUMAN-PIPING-20